      "writtenOn": "2021-02-11T14:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was a not very good attempt to describe the various special cases in connectivity APIs that check mLockdownEnabled.\n\nWe\u0027ve already deleted one of them, which is that when legacy lockdown is on, VPNs could not call setUnderlyingNetworks.\n\nThe remaining one is that when a legacy lockdown VPN is enabled, the legacy NetworkInfo-based APIs, and getDefaultNetworkCapabilitiesForUser which is used by statusbar, behave as though VPNs didn\u0027t have underlying networks. \n\nI\u0027m not sure that these special cases still make sense though, so maybe we can delete them in S. Removed this bullet point in the hope that we can do that.",
      "parentUuid": "76448d82_0f737e8c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1241,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 1241,
