      "writtenOn": "2021-02-11T14:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Legacy VPN\" !\u003d \"legacy lockdown VPN\". Here I\u0027m just talking about LegacyLockdownTracker. We *could* fix legacy VPN to do this as well, and I think doing so would be more correct, but I don\u0027t know if it\u0027s worth it.\n\nAs for why I think we need to pass this in, I think that\u0027s the same question as your other comment https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/1553463/comment/230141e4_edf7ff89/ , right?\n\nIf so, I think the answer is: it makes things marginally more correct, and there doesn\u0027t seem to be any reason not to do that.",
